    "show_share": true,
    "description": "After years working in the media industry, Faith Oneya, an Editor at the Daily Nation decided to pursue AKU's Master of Arts in Digital Journalism programme. Before her rise to news editor, she worked in the digital media department which gave her a taste of the new and dynamic field in media. Her experience there also led her to question the opportunities available for women in digital media - a query that moved her to conduct research as part of her studies. She shares more on her journey and the impact the programme had on her career.",
